invariant: INV-7
file: suite.h
catches: srv_flight_test_aes
reason: srv_first_offered_suite takes the first suite in the server's order whether
  or not the client listed it, so a client that offers AES-GCM alone is
  answered with ChaCha20, and one that offers nothing this build holds
  gets a suite instead of handshake_failure. RFC 9846 §4.2.3 makes a
  suite the client did not offer an abort on the client's side, so the
  server must never name one. The flight test's hello with no suite
  expects handshake_failure; srv_select_suite proves the same rule.

--- old
        if ((offered & srv_suite_bit(order[i])) != 0) {
--- new
        if ((offered & srv_suite_bit(order[i])) != 0 || i == 0) {
